# AGENTS.layers.example: format reference for the configuration layer manifest.
#
# Downstream repos copy this file to AGENTS.layers (committed) and edit it.
# Upstream project-noemi/agents ships no live AGENTS.layers.
#
# Rules (enforced by `npm run audit`):
#   - one repo-relative path per line; `#` starts a comment
#   - no absolute paths, no `~`, no `..`, no whitespace, no leading `@`
#   - markdown files only (.md)
#   - do not list AGENTS.md (always first), AGENTS.local.md (always last),
#     or AGENTS.override.md (Codex treats it as a replacement, not a layer)
#
# Order is precedence: AGENTS.md loads first, then these lines top to bottom,
# then AGENTS.local.md. Later sources win on conflict. A listed file that does
# not exist is skipped, so a layer may be listed before it is vendored in.
#
# NOEMI_ORG_LAYERS="a.md,b.md" replaces this list for one session (CI, tests).
#
# Layers may replace preference rules (mark them with
# <!-- override: <rule-id> relax -->). Core rules (secrets.*, refusal.*) can
# only be clarified or tightened; any attempt to relax one fails the audit.
#
# After editing AGENTS.layers, run `npm run generate` and commit CLAUDE.md and
# GEMINI.md so Claude Code and Gemini CLI import the same stack.

# 1. MSP / MSSP layer: owned by the managing company, vendored read-only
#    (see docs/configuration-layers.md, "How an MSP adds its layer").
org/example-msp/AGENTS.md

# 2. Customer layer: owned by this repository.
org/example-customer/AGENTS.md

# To try the upstream template as a layer, uncomment:
# org/example/AGENTS.md
